    accessibility: ["Tone is announced through a text status word (\"On target\", \"At risk\", \"Off track\") next to the color, never the color alone", "Value and Target are both always visible as text, so \"how far off\" is readable without comparing two colors by eye", "ShowTrend's sparkline is decorative; the same direction it shows is already stated by Tone's text status", "The Export action carries a real accessible name (\"Export scorecard\"), not an icon-only affordance"],
    limitations: ["Tone is computed from Value vs. Target by the host before it reaches the component — the component itself has no notion of what a metric's Red/Amber/Green thresholds should be", "Best for a double-digit number of metrics; past roughly 20, Data Table's own card view reads better", "OnExport only ever hands back the current data — turning that into an actual PDF or Excel file is the host's own job via Power Apps' PDF() function or Export-to-Excel capability, not something this component does itself"],
